  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Amtec has $283M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Amtec received 15 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $18.9M. Obligations are down 29.5% year over year. Historic obligations show variability: FY21 obligated $248M, FY22 obligated $70.4M, FY23 obligated $138M, FY24 obligated $513M, and FY25 obligated $401M. The current-year total is partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date. These figures are contract obligations except where award-value notes are explicitly identified as total contract values. The sequence of fiscal-year obligations highlights swings in contracting volume that contractors and procurement officers should note when benchmarking Amtec against peers or evaluating capture strategies. Use the year-by-year obligations to guide questions about program continuity, award timing, and potential capacity for follow-on work during FY2026 to date.",
